.TH CRAFT 6 "November 2026" "craft 3.5.1" "Games"
.SH NAME
craft \- CRAFT: The Vicious Vikings, a real-time strategy game for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B craft
.RB [ \-scale
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B craft
is a real-time strategy game in the style of Warcraft and Dune II.
As a Viking king, you build up a settlement, feed up to 70 citizens,
harvest gold and wood, trade, and train knights, archers, catapults and
ships to conquer the computer players' islands.
.PP
A start menu lets you choose the world (with or without islands,
local sight, a king unit, random seed), the human and computer players,
and their settings.
Press
.B Play
to start.
.PP
Press
.B save
during a game to save it, and
.B restore
in the start menu to continue a saved game.
.PP
On large screens the game is zoomed (1.25\(mu, 1.5\(mu, 2\(mu or 3\(mu).
By default the largest step that fits the screen is used; change it
with the zoom buttons on the start menu's
.B Details
page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-scale " N"
Zoom the game
.I N
times (1 to 4, for example 1.5) for this run only, instead of the zoom
set in the start menu.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
The X display to use.
.TP
.B CRAFT_DATADIR
Directory that holds the game data
.RI ( hcraft/ ,
.IR buttons/ " and"
.IR .windefaults.params ).
If unset,
.B craft
uses the current directory when it holds the data, and otherwise the
installed data directory.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Saved games are kept in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/craft/saves ,
by default
.IR ~/.local/share/craft/saves .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The zoom setting is kept in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/craft/settings ,
by default
.IR ~/.config/craft/settings .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/craft/
Installed pictures, button icons and window defaults.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/doc/craft/html/craft.html
The original game manual: units, buildings and orders.
.SH SEE ALSO
The art tools
.BR craft\-cmedit ,
.BR craft\-ppm2cmap ,
.BR craft\-mirror ,
.BR craft\-split ,
.BR craft\-recolor ,
.BR craft\-shade ,
.BR craft\-medit ,
.BR craft\-morph " and"
.BR craft\-compress
are described in README.md.
